<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saada</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sa'dah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saada is a city in the far north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> and capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saada-governorate">Saada Governorate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-hadi-ila-l-haqq-yahya">Yahya ibn al-Husayn</a> founded the Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">imamate</a> there in 897, and it remained the religious heart of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaydism">Zaydism</a>, with the mosque that holds his tomb. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> walls and tower houses are well known. Since 2004 it has been the stronghold of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/houthi-movement">Houthi movement</a> and has suffered heavily in the wars since then.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saada.jpg" alt="Saada" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sa%27dah_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
